Z||000000||johnt671||03-22-2001||07:34 PM||||Have an 84 4 cyl w/air and two speed fan.  finally found the fan switch and odered one from Rodney Dickman.  Problem is I have a partly melted lite blue conn. w/ a green/white wire and a green/black wire.  Haynes shows this going to a larger fan switch and then a single grn/wht wire going to a smaller far switch. I can&lt;t find the switch that the two wire conn. goes to or the single grn/wht wire that goes to Rodney's switch.  I'm about to give up and just wire in an off/on switch.  Checked ogre's cave and he also said there are two switchs with the 2 spd fan.  It would be great if anyone could help.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||03-22-2001||07:44 PM||||Yes. there are 2 switches.<P>The 2 speed fan low speed turn on is about 218F. More than low enough. If it's not comming on then the switch is bad or there is some other problem.<P>Your new switch will replace the single contact 235F switch. This will effect only the low speed of the fan.<P>The wiring for this is in the haynes book, etc. ||||reg||1
